    <section class="section fade-up fade-up-2">
        <p>Parachute is open source. The most direct way to read about how it works is in the code itself &mdash; start with each repo's <code>README.md</code>. Below are the design notes that anchor architectural direction post-launch.</p>
    </section>

    <section class="section">
        <h2>Architecture design notes</h2>
        <p>Written 2026-04-20 in the week before public launch, capturing the shape Parachute is evolving toward.</p>
        <ul class="blog-list">
            <li>
                <a href="https://github.com/ParachuteComputer/parachute.computer/blob/main/design/2026-04-20-module-architecture.md" class="blog-post-card" target="_blank">
                    <h3>Module architecture</h3>
                    <div class="date">2026-04-20</div>
                    <p class="excerpt">The canonical module protocol: <code>info</code>, <code>config</code>, <code>services.json</code>, <code>.well-known/parachute.json</code>. How Vault, Lens, Scribe, and third-party modules plug into a single ecosystem under one HTTPS URL.</p>
                </a>
            </li>
            <li>
                <a href="https://github.com/ParachuteComputer/parachute.computer/blob/main/design/2026-04-20-hub-as-portal-oauth-and-service-catalog.md" class="blog-post-card" target="_blank">
                    <h3>Hub as portal &mdash; OAuth and the service catalog</h3>
                    <div class="date">2026-04-20</div>
                    <p class="excerpt">OAuth architecture with the hub as issuer. One ecosystem sign-in, tokens carrying a service catalog, scopes that constrain what a client can reach.</p>
                </a>
            </li>
            <li>
                <a href="https://github.com/ParachuteComputer/parachute.computer/blob/main/design/2026-04-20-cloud-offering-sketch.md" class="blog-post-card" target="_blank">
                    <h3>Parachute Cloud &mdash; architecture sketch</h3>
                    <div class="date">2026-04-20</div>
                    <p class="excerpt">Cloud deployment shape: tenant-per-subdomain, Postgres-backed, CDN-hosted Lens, pooled Scribe. A plausible north star we refine when a first cloud user materializes.</p>
                </a>
            </li>
        </ul>
    </section>

    <section class="section">
        <h2>Per-repo READMEs</h2>
        <ul>
            <li><a href="https://github.com/ParachuteComputer/parachute-cli" target="_blank"><strong>parachute-cli</strong></a> &mdash; the coordinator: <code>install</code>, <code>start</code>, <code>stop</code>, <code>expose</code>, and lifecycle for every module.</li>
            <li><a href="https://github.com/ParachuteComputer/parachute-vault" target="_blank"><strong>parachute-vault</strong></a> &mdash; the knowledge graph. REST + MCP, SQLite-backed.</li>
            <li><a href="https://github.com/ParachuteComputer/parachute-lens" target="_blank"><strong>parachute-lens</strong></a> &mdash; browser-based companion for your vault. Installable PWA.</li>
            <li><a href="https://github.com/ParachuteComputer/parachute-scribe" target="_blank"><strong>parachute-scribe</strong></a> &mdash; Whisper-compatible transcription API.</li>
            <li><a href="https://github.com/ParachuteComputer/parachute-channel" target="_blank"><strong>parachute-channel</strong></a> &mdash; messaging gateway for Claude Code agents.</li>
            <li><a href="https://github.com/ParachuteComputer/parachute-patterns" target="_blank"><strong>parachute-patterns</strong></a> &mdash; cross-repo conventions (naming, schemas, OAuth scopes, ports).</li>
        </ul>
    </section>

